    "sample_text2.txt": {
      "path": "data/ner_samples\\sample_text2.txt",
      "language": "en",
      "translated": false,
      "text_used": "On 15 June 2026 at 23:47 UTC, Colonel Sarah Mitchell, a British officer assigned to the NATO Rapid Response Command, directed elements of the 2nd Mechanized Battalion during Operation Silent Horizon after intelligence reports indicated suspicious activity near Forward Operating Base Sentinel located in the Al-Qamar region at coordinates 31.7683°N, 35.2137°E. The battalion, supported by two M142 HIMARS weapon systems mounted on Oshkosh FMTV vehicles and escorted by AH-64 Apache aircraft operating under communication identifiers FALCON-11 and FALCON-12, was tasked with securing a logistics facility known as Depot Echo. Simultaneously, the USS Arlington, a San Antonio-class vessel positioned 45 nautical miles offshore, relayed surveillance data collected from AN/PRC-158 tactical radios and MQ-9 Reaper reconnaissance assets to the Joint Intelligence Directorate. During the operation, Major Ahmed Al-Rashid of the Royal Jordanian Armed Forces reported that an unidentified convoy had departed from Camp Al-Hadeed at 21:15 local time and was moving toward Checkpoint Delta-7. The resulting event triggered an emergency coordination meeting between NATO Rapid Response Command, the Joint Intelligence Directorate, and the 5th Armored Brigade, leading to the deployment of additional Leopard 2A7 vehicles and counter-drone equipment. By 02:10 UTC on 16 June 2026, all objectives of Operation Silent Horizon had been completed, and communication identifier SIERRA-NET-09 confirmed mission success.",
      "original_text": "On 15 June 2026 at 23:47 UTC, Colonel Sarah Mitchell, a British officer assigned to the NATO Rapid Response Command, directed elements of the 2nd Mechanized Battalion during Operation Silent Horizon after intelligence reports indicated suspicious activity near Forward Operating Base Sentinel located in the Al-Qamar region at coordinates 31.7683°N, 35.2137°E. The battalion, supported by two M142 HIMARS weapon systems mounted on Oshkosh FMTV vehicles and escorted by AH-64 Apache aircraft operating under communication identifiers FALCON-11 and FALCON-12, was tasked with securing a logistics facility known as Depot Echo. Simultaneously, the USS Arlington, a San Antonio-class vessel positioned 45 nautical miles offshore, relayed surveillance data collected from AN/PRC-158 tactical radios and MQ-9 Reaper reconnaissance assets to the Joint Intelligence Directorate. During the operation, Major Ahmed Al-Rashid of the Royal Jordanian Armed Forces reported that an unidentified convoy had departed from Camp Al-Hadeed at 21:15 local time and was moving toward Checkpoint Delta-7. The resulting event triggered an emergency coordination meeting between NATO Rapid Response Command, the Joint Intelligence Directorate, and the 5th Armored Brigade, leading to the deployment of additional Leopard 2A7 vehicles and counter-drone equipment. By 02:10 UTC on 16 June 2026, all objectives of Operation Silent Horizon had been completed, and communication identifier SIERRA-NET-09 confirmed mission success.",
